    {
      "id": "skarn_ruvo_maps_told",
      "says": [
        {
          "text": "“To the inch.” He is proud of it and then he is not. “Every hole, every seam, every fault, since the founding. I have seen the sheets — my father cut plate for the cases they keep them in.” A look toward the shoulder. “And the shoulder sheet stops at that mouth. Clean. No note. The hold *always* notes.”"
        }
      ],
